messages.content:
You are supporting a process mining research prototype.
Use only the synthetic scenario information provided below.
Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: S07
Scenario title: Meeting Summary and Email Reporting
Initial workflow description:
After a meeting, the contents are summarized and shared by email with the relevant people.

Clarification questions:
[
  {
    "id": "Q1",
    "question": "What event or action currently starts the summarization process after a meeting ends — for example, does a specific person manually initiate it, or is it triggered automatically by a system such as a calendar or conferencing tool?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q2",
    "question": "How is the meeting summary currently created — is it written manually by a participant, derived from a recorded transcript, or generated with the help of an automated or AI-based tool?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q3",
    "question": "How is the list of email recipients determined — is it always the set of meeting attendees, a predefined distribution list, or does the sender decide case by case?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q4",
    "question": "Does the summary need to be reviewed or approved by anyone before the email is sent, and if so, who holds that responsibility?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q5",
    "question": "What content is expected to appear in the summary email — for instance, is it a free-form narrative, or must it include structured elements such as action items, owners, and deadlines?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q6",
    "question": "Is there a target or maximum time limit within which the summary email must be sent after the meeting concludes?"
  }
]
Reference workflow for oracle use:
{
  "goal": "Summarize meeting content and distribute decisions, owners, and deadlines to relevant stakeholders.",
  "actors": [
    "meeting participant",
    "minute taker",
    "decision owner",
    "recipient"
  ],
  "systems": [
    "calendar system",
    "meeting transcript or notes",
    "email client",
    "task tracker"
  ],
  "inputs": [
    "meeting agenda",
    "meeting notes or transcript",
    "participant list",
    "action-item list"
  ],
  "outputs": [
    "meeting summary email",
    "decision list",
    "action-item assignments",
    "task tracker updates"
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "name": "Collect meeting notes or transcript",
      "actor": "minute taker"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "name": "Extract decisions and action items",
      "actor": "minute taker"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "name": "Confirm unclear items with decision owners",
      "actor": "minute taker"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "name": "Draft summary email",
      "actor": "minute taker"
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "name": "Attach or link supporting materials",
      "actor": "minute taker"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6",
      "name": "Send email to relevant recipients",
      "actor": "minute taker"
    },
    {
      "id": "A7",
      "name": "Update task tracker if needed",
      "actor": "decision owner"
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "id": "D1",
      "condition": "Are all action items assigned to owners?",
      "branches": [
        "assigned",
        "clarification needed"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "condition": "Does the meeting require task tracking?",
      "branches": [
        "tracker update needed",
        "email only"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exceptions": [
    "missing transcript",
    "unclear decision owner",
    "recipient list incomplete",
    "confidential content included"
  ],
  "dependencies": [
    {
      "from": "A1",
      "to": "A2",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A2",
      "to": "A3",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A3",
      "to": "A4",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A4",
      "to": "A5",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A5",
      "to": "A6",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A6",
      "to": "A7",
      "type": "control_flow"
    }
  ],
  "automation_opportunities": [
    {
      "target": "A2",
      "rationale": "Decision and action-item extraction can be supported by summarization models."
    },
    {
      "target": "A4",
      "rationale": "Email drafting can be template-based."
    },
    {
      "target": "A7",
      "rationale": "Task tracker updates can be generated from action-item tables."
    }
  ]
}
Task: Simulate a concise domain expert who answers only these questions using the reference workflow.
Do not reveal the full reference workflow. Do not add details not needed by the questions.
If a requested fact is absent, explicitly say it is not specified; do not guess.
Use at most 80 words per answer. Return one answer for each question, with matching ID and question text.
Return JSON: {"answers": [{"question_id": "Q1", "question": "original question", "answer": "grounded answer"}]}

Additional constraint for this respondent: this expert answers vaguely and never commits to specifics.
Do not name any actor, system, artifact, threshold, condition or exception from the reference workflow.
Use hedged generalities such as "the person in charge usually checks it before it goes out".
Answer every question in this style, at most 30 words each.
